From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Jun Matsushita <jun@mercury.com>
Date: Wed, 4 Nov 2026 17:39:42 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 2/5] buck2: name actions in RE request metadata, and record
 the data a BEP stream needs

Two changes to core crates that the OSS build event service sink builds on.
Each is useful without it.

RE requests carry the action's identity. ReActionIdentity gains the action
id (the action digest), mnemonic (the action category), target id and
configuration id, and the OSS client puts them in RequestMetadata. This
covers executions, action cache lookups and writes, and uploads. Callers
without an identity pass None. Servers such as BuildBuddy then show these
per action.

Events carry what a Bazel Build Event Protocol stream reports and Buck2's
events left out:
- an action's outputs (path, digest, size, kind) and output symlinks;
- a test suite's labels and a test's timeout;
- a materialization's URL;
- `buck2 run`'s final command line (RunExecRequest);
- fetches made by git-backed external cells (ExternalResourceFetch);
- the repository root and working directory in the invocation metadata.

Existing consumers see only new fields and new event variants.

Assisted-by: Claude:claude-opus-5-5
